amux repo — track the repositories agents get worktrees of

usage: amux repo <command>

commands:
  add [<src>]            track a repo: a gh owner/name slug, a git URL, or a local path
  ls                     list tracked repositories
  rm <name>              stop tracking a repository
  set <agent> <repo>...  re-scope an agent to exactly these tracked repos
  grant <coordinator> [--all | --none | repo...]
                         set a workgroup's repo ceiling (host only)

Run 'amux repo <command> --help' for details.
